# Example only. Never installed by mascot-wardrobe.
# Publishes ONE saved closet look, chosen by the weather category of the country profile, as the
# WhatsApp profile photo. It reads the temperature from the state file your own weather updater
# already writes (temperature_c + updated_at_utc), so it makes no weather request and needs no
# coordinates. Nothing here is enabled by this repository: copy and adapt it yourself.
#
# Review-only dry-run example. No schedule is installed or changed. After parity and visual
# review, explicitly appending --apply permits the selected live effects.
# The closet is only read: it is not regenerated, edited, re-inventoried or switched to the saved
# wardrobe. If the state file is stale or malformed the command exits 2 and changes nothing.
#
# Credentials live outside the repository: the EnvironmentFile (mode 0600, yours) holds
#   MASCOT_WARDROBE_WHATSAPP_BRIDGE_HEADER=<Name: value required by your bridge>
# Run this on the machine that hosts the bridge: the bridge listens on loopback only.
#
# Test first, with no --apply (a dry-run prints the plan and writes nothing):
#   mascot-wardrobe publish-closet --closet-root /path/to/closet --wardrobe my-looks --country BR \
#     --state-file /path/to/weather/state.json
#     --whatsapp-catalog-dir /path/to/bridge/approved-photos \
#     --whatsapp-state-dir /path/to/private/whatsapp-state
# Optional: --overlay /path/to/your-overlay.png (square RGBA PNG you supply; it is clipped to the
# circular-safe area) and --background '#102b32'.
# Existing-service review (requires separate approval; do not install this file automatically):
# The old sync_avatar.py post-hook can overwrite the new WhatsApp photo. In a separately reviewed
# drop-in for THAT service, first clear ALL inherited post-hooks, then replace with the publisher:
#   [Service]
#   ExecStartPost=
#   ExecStartPost=/path/to/venv/bin/mascot-wardrobe publish-closet --country BR --state-file /path/to/weather/state.json
# Keep this dry-run until delivery and candidates are approved. If using a standalone publisher
# service instead, disable/remove the old avatar post-hook before enabling it; do not run both.
# Review the old badge pre-hook and updater separately: they can still mutate installed Hermes pets.
# Do not clear the weather producer blindly; establish a read-only fresh-state hand-off first.
# Current location/cadence remain unresolved. No real location/account is configured here.
# Rollback: remove the reviewed drop-in, restore the old hook if intended, and separately restore
# the previous Hermes slug/photo from verified state/backup. Removing a unit does not restore photos.
[Unit]
Description=Publish the weather-selected closet look to WhatsApp (example)

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=/path/to/workdir
EnvironmentFile=/path/to/private/mascot-wardrobe.env
ExecStart=/path/to/venv/bin/mascot-wardrobe publish-closet \
  --closet-root /path/to/closet --wardrobe my-looks --country BR \
  --state-file /path/to/weather/state.json \
  --whatsapp-catalog-dir /path/to/bridge/approved-photos \
  --whatsapp-state-dir /path/to/private/whatsapp-state \
  --whatsapp-bridge-url http://127.0.0.1:3000
